## What changed

**New module `src/tokenize.ts`** — exports `tokenize(text): string[]`, containing exactly `wordCount`'s old logic: lower-case, split on runs of anything that is not a letter, digit or apostrophe, drop empty words.

**`src/stats.ts`** — both functions now go through `tokenize`:
- `wordCount` is now `tokenize(text).length`; its results are unchanged (same lower-case + split on `[^a-z0-9']+`), and I added a test pinning that a word like `hello,world` still counts as two tokens.
- `topWords` now counts the lower-cased tokens, so `'The'` and `'the'` no longer differ, and returns the words lower-cased. Sorting is count descending, ties broken alphabetically (the old code had no tie-break at all).

**Tests** — a new `src/tokenize.test.ts` (splitting, apostrophes, digits, no empty words) and additions to `src/stats.test.ts` (most-frequent-first, case-insensitivity + lower-cased output, alphabetical tie-breaks, `n` respected, unchanged `wordCount` behaviour).

## Checks

`bun test` (the only script in package.json — there's no lint or typecheck step):

